normalize_fdm: don't dereference a missing nozzle_diameter when clamping
wipe_tower_filament.

DynamicPrintConfig::normalize_fdm runs on PARTIAL configs: the CLI
normalizes each --load-settings file on its own, and
PrintObject::object_config_from_model_object normalizes per-object
configs. wipe_tower_filament is a process key; nozzle_diameter is a
machine key — so a process preset containing wipe_tower_filament (ANY
value) hits `this->opt<ConfigOptionFloats>("nozzle_diameter")->size()`
with a null option and segfaults the config loader.

Reproduced against the 2.3.4 CLI: a process JSON with
wipe_tower_filament="0" → SIGSEGV; same file plus nozzle_diameter →
slices fine; wipe_tower_filament="1" without nozzle_diameter → SIGSEGV
(the value is irrelevant, presence in a partial config is the trigger).

Guard on nozzle_diameter being present; the clamp is re-evaluated later
during full-config normalization where the nozzle count is known.

Retire-if: upstream Snapmaker Orca guards this block (or normalize_fdm
stops running on partial configs).

---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp b/src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
index c0a2676..198dd33 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp
@@ -7379,8 +7379,15 @@ void DynamicPrintConfig::normalize_fdm(int used_filaments)
         }
     }
 
-    if (this->has("wipe_tower_filament")) {
+    if (this->has("wipe_tower_filament") && this->has("nozzle_diameter")) {
         // If invalid, replace with 0.
+        // OrcaXR: guard on nozzle_diameter being present — normalize_fdm
+        // also runs on PARTIAL configs (a process preset loaded on its own
+        // by the CLI, a per-object config), where the unguarded
+        // opt("nozzle_diameter")->size() dereferences a null option and
+        // segfaults the config loader. Without the machine's nozzle count
+        // the clamp cannot be evaluated; leave the value for the full-config
+        // normalization to validate.
         int extruder      = this->opt<ConfigOptionInt>("wipe_tower_filament")->value;
         int num_extruders = this->opt<ConfigOptionFloats>("nozzle_diameter")->size();
         if (extruder < 0 || extruder > num_extruders)
